### Static rendering enforcement for output: export

Source: https://github.com/vercel/next.js/blob/canary/packages/next/src/server/app-render/create-component-tree.tsx

When `output: 'export'` is configured, any page without an explicit `dynamic` setting is forced to `'error'` mode (making any dynamic API access a build error), and `dynamic = 'force-dynamic'` throws a `StaticGenBailoutError` because no runtime server exists to dynamically render routes. This is the only topic among the user's four questions that has explicit source code enforcement — Client Components, CSS Modules, and browser-only effects have no specific constraints in the source code under `output: export`.

```typescript
  if (nextConfigOutput === 'export') {
    if (!dynamic || dynamic === 'auto') {
      dynamic = 'error'
    } else if (dynamic === 'force-dynamic') {
      // force-dynamic is always incompatible with 'export'. We must interrupt the build
      throw new StaticGenBailoutError(
        `Page with \`dynamic = "force-dynamic"\` couldn't be exported. \`output: "export"\` requires all pages be renderable statically because there is no runtime server to dynamically render routes in this output format. Learn more: https://nextjs.org/docs/app/building-your-application/deploying/static-exports`
      )
    }
  }
```

