### output: 'export' constraint — no server image optimization

Source: https://github.com/vercel/next.js/blob/canary/packages/next/src/shared/lib/get-img-props.ts

With `output: 'export'`, the server-side Image Optimization API is unavailable. This forces all image processing to happen client-side in a local-only architecture. The error advises either removing `output: 'export'` or setting `images.unoptimized: true`.

```typescript
    if (config.output === 'export' && isDefaultLoader && !unoptimized) {
      throw new Error(
        `Image Optimization using the default loader is not compatible with \`{ output: 'export' }\`.
  Possible solutions:
    - Remove \`{ output: 'export' }\` and run "next start" to run server mode including the Image Optimization API.
    - Configure \`{ images: { unoptimized: true } }\` in \`next.config.js\` to disable the Image Optimization API.
  Read more: https://nextjs.org/docs/messages/export-image-api`
      )
    }
```

